messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 149 and 173?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 060 and 056, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 335 by 981. This can be done by multiplying 236 by 20 and then by 77.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 074 by 6.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together to get the final product.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **149** and **173**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n\\[.\n149 \\times 173.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Break down the multiplication using the distributive property.\n\n\\[.\n149 \\times 173 = 149 \\times (170 + 3) = (149 \\times 170) + (149 \\times 3).\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Calculate each part separately.\n\n1. **Calculate \\(149 \\times 170\\):**.\n\n\\[.\n149 \\times 170 = 149 \\times (17 \\times 10) = (149 \\times 17) \\times 10.\n\\].\n\nFirst, find \\(149 \\times 17\\):.\n\n\\[.\n149 \\times 17 = 2533.\n\\].\n\nThen multiply by 10:.\n\n\\[.\n2533 \\times 10 = 25330.\n\\].\n\n2. **Calculate \\(149 \\times 3\\):**.\n\n\\[.\n149 \\times 3 = 447.\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Add the two results together.\n\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
