messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 260 and 305?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 597 and 621, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 338 as 731 plus 48, and 733 as 474 plus 1.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 074 by each part of 190.\n\nThis will give me four separate multiplication problems: 335 times 272, 358 times 1, 45 times 844, and 96 times 0.\n\nAfter calculating each of these, I'll add all the results together to find the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **260** and **305**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n260 = 200 + 60\n\\]\n\\[\n305 = 300 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n260 \\times 305 = (200 + 60) \\times (300 + 5)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 200 \\times 300 + 200 \\times 5 + 60 \\times 300 + 60 \\times 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(200 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 300 = 60,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(200 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 5 = 1,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(60 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 300 = 18,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(60 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 5 = 300\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Results Together\n\n\\[\n60,\\!000 + 1,\\!000 + 18,\\!000 + 300 = 79,\\!300\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{79,\\!300}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
