messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 628 and 561?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 499 and 212, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 402 by 426. This is straightforward since multiplying by 889 is simple, and then I can adjust for the 6.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 506 by 81. This involves multiplying 531 by 3 and then adding two zeros to account for the 73.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 113 by 9, which is just 850 itself.\n\nAfter calculating each of these parts, I'll add them all together to get the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **628** and **561**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n628 \\times 561 &= 628 \\times (500 + 60 + 1) \\\\\n&= 628 \\times 500 + 628 \\times 60 + 628 \\times 1 \\\\\n&= 314,\\!000 + 37,\\!680 + 628 \\\\\n&= 314,\\!000 + 37,\\!680 \\\\\n&= 351,\\!680 \\\\\n&= 351,\\!680 + 628 \\\\\n&= 352,\\!308\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{352,\\!308}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
