messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 746 and 536?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 027 and 685, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values. \n\nFirst, I'll express 871 as 977 + 75 + 7 and 319 as 143 + 63 + 7. \n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 483 by each part of 787. This means I'll calculate 233 multiplied by 936, 399 multiplied by 66, 219 multiplied by 9, and so on for each component.\n\nAfter calculating all these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I don't miss any part of the multiplication and helps in keeping track of the calculations accurately.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **746** and **536**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}746 \\\\\n\\times\\phantom{0}536 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1: Multiply 746 by 6 (units place of 536)**\n\n\\[\n746 \\times 6 = 4,\\!476\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply 746 by 30 (tens place of 536)**\n\n\\[\n746 \\times 30 = 22,\\!380\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Multiply 746 by 500 (hundreds place of 536)**\n\n\\[\n746 \\times 500 = 373,\\!000\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Add all the results together**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}4,\\!476 \\\\\n+22,\\!380 \\\\\n+373,\\!000 \\\\\n\\hline\n400,\\!856 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{400,\\!856}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
