messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 220 and 776?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 009 and 093, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 761 as 139 + 98 and 112 as 641 + 19 + 0.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 397 by each part of 232.\n\nThis will give me several multiplication steps: 454 multiplied by 055, 672 multiplied by 69, 428 multiplied by 4, 57 multiplied by 967, 07 multiplied by 14, and 19 multiplied by 8.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n\nFinally, I'll sum all these values to find the total product of 516 and 247.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **220** and **776**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n220 \\times 776 = (200 + 20) \\times (700 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n200 \\times 700 &= 140,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 70 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 6 &= 1,\\!200 \\\\\n20 \\times 700 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n20 \\times 70 &= 1,\\!400 \\\\\n20 \\times 6 &= 120 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nSum all the results from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n140,\\!000 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!200 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!400 + 120 = 170,\\!720\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{170,\\!720}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
