messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 171 and 271?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 715 and 466, I'll start by breaking down the numbers to make the multiplication easier.\n\nFirst, I'll separate 497 into 637, 57, and 3. This allows me to multiply each part individually.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 326 by each of these components: 152, 31, and 8.\n\nAfter calculating each part, I'll add the results together to get the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **171** and **271**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nSplit **271** into **200**, **70**, and **1** to simplify the multiplication.\n\n\\[\n171 \\times 271 = 171 \\times (200 + 70 + 1)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nMultiply **171** by each of the split parts.\n\n1. **Multiply by 200:**\n   \\[\n   171 \\times 200 = 34,\\!200\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 70:**\n   \\[\n   171 \\times 70 = 11,\\!970\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 1:**\n   \\[\n   171 \\times 1 = 171\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results Together\nSum up all the products from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n34,\\!200 + 11,\\!970 + 171 = 46,\\!341\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{46,\\!341}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
