messages:   57%|#####7    | 287/500 [05:17<00:34,  6.14it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 684 and 663?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 846 and 181, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values. \n\nFirst, I'll express 557 as 381 + 18 + 7 and 976 as 449 + 72 + 7. \n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This means I'll calculate 096 multiplied by 248, 352 multiplied by 93, 166 multiplied by 1, and so on for each component.\n\nAfter calculating all these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I don't miss any part of the multiplication and helps in accurately finding the product of 025 and 441.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **684** and **663**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's express both numbers in terms of their place values:\n\n\\[\n684 = 600 + 80 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n663 = 600 + 60 + 3\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nWe'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n684 \\times 663 &= (600 + 80 + 4) \\times (600 + 60 + 3) \\\\\n&= 600 \\times 600 + 600 \\times 60 + 600 \\times 3 \\\\\n&\\quad + 80 \\times 600 + 80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 3 \\\\\n&\\quad + 4 \\times 600 + 4 \\times 60 + 4 \\times 3\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Multiplication\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n600 \\times 600 &= 360,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 60 &= 36,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 3 &= 1,\\!800 \\\\\n80 \\times 600 &= 48,\\!000 \\\\\n80 \\times 60 &= 4,\\!800 \\\\\n80 \\times 3 &= 240 \\\\\n4 \\times 600 &= 2,\\!400 \\\\\n4 \\times 60 &= 240 \\\\\n4 \\times 3 &= 12 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n360,\\!000 &+ 36,\\!000 + 1,\\!800 \\\\\n&+ 48,\\!000 + 4,\\!800 + 240 \\\\\n&+ 2,\\!400 + 240 + 12 \\\\\n&= 360,\\!000 + 36,\\!000 = 396,\\!000 \\\\\n396,\\!000 + 1,\\!800 &= 397,\\!800 \\\\\n397,\\!800 + 48,\\!000 &= 445,\\!800 \\\\\n445,\\!800 + 4,\\!800 &= 450,\\!600 \\\\\n450,\\!600 + 240 &= 450,\\!840 \\\\\n450,\\!840 + 2,\\!400 &= 453,\\!240 \\\\\n453,\\!240 + 240 &= 453,\\!480 \\\\\n453,\\!480 + 12 &= 453,\\!492 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{453,\\!492}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
