messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 355 and 375?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 693 and 928, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 569 as 846 + 86 + 9 and 797 as 128 + 68 + 8.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\nThis will give me several multiplication terms that I'll calculate individually.\n\nAfter obtaining all the products, I'll add them together to get the final result.\n\nFinally, I'll sum all these terms to find the total product of 498 and 668.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **355** and **375**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n355 = 300 + 50 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n355 \\times 375 = (300 + 50 + 5) \\times (300 + 70 + 5)\n\\]\n\nThis expands to:\n\n\\[\n300 \\times 300 + 300 \\times 70 + 300 \\times 5 + 50 \\times 300 + 50 \\times 70 + 50 \\times 5 + 5 \\times 300 + 5 \\times 70 + 5 \\times 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Term\n\n1. \\( 300 \\times 300 = 90,\\!000 \\)\n2. \\( 300 \\times 70 = 21,\\!000 \\)\n3. \\( 300 \\times 5 = 1,\\!500 \\)\n4. \\( 50 \\times 300 = 15,\\!000 \\)\n5. \\( 50 \\times 70 = 3,\\!500 \\)\n6. \\( 50 \\times 5 = 250 \\)\n7. \\( 5 \\times 300 = 1,\\!500 \\)\n8. \\( 5 \\times 70 = 350 \\)\n9. \\( 5 \\times 5 = 25 \\)\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Terms Together\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 + 3,\\!500 + 250 + 1,\\!500 + 350 + 25\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 = 111,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n111,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 = 112,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n112,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 = 127,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n127,\\!500 + 3,\\!500 = 131,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n131,\\!000 + 250 = 131,\\!250\n\\]\n\\[\n131,\\!250 + 1,\\!500 = 132,\\!750\n\\]\n\\[\n132,\\!750 + 350 = 133,\\!100\n\\]\n\\[\n133,\\!100 + 25 = 133,\\!125\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{133,\\!125}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
