messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 947 and 988?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 104 and 359, I'll start by breaking down the numbers to make the multiplication easier.\n\nFirst, I'll express 416 as 0436 minus 54. This allows me to use the distributive property.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 569 by 6762, which is straightforward since multiplying by 8466 simply adds three zeros to the end of the number.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 668 by 26. To do this, I'll break down 35 into 85 and 5, making the multiplication simpler.\n\nAfter calculating both parts, I'll subtract the second result from the first to get the final product.\n\nFinally, I'll add all the components together to find the total product of 856 and 729.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **947** and **988**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n947 \\times 988 &= 947 \\times (1000 - 12) \\\\.\n&= 947 \\times 1000 - 947 \\times 12 \\\\.\n&= 947,000 - (947 \\times 10 + 947 \\times 2) \\\\.\n&= 947,000 - (9,470 + 1,894) \\\\.\n&= 947,000 - 11,364 \\\\.\n&= 935,636.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
